# The Obby extensions: named modes, the command list, a link preview, channel-bots, the WHOIS
# batch and voice signalling.
< :irc.example.org CAP * LS :message-tags server-time batch draft/named-modes obsidianirc/cmdslist obby.world/whois obby.world/channel-bots draft/bot-cmds obsidianirc/voice
< :irc.example.org CAP * ACK :message-tags
< :irc.example.org CAP * ACK :server-time
< :irc.example.org CAP * ACK :batch
< :irc.example.org CAP * ACK :draft/named-modes
< :irc.example.org CAP * ACK :obsidianirc/cmdslist
< :irc.example.org CAP * ACK :obby.world/whois
< :irc.example.org CAP * ACK :obby.world/channel-bots
< :irc.example.org CAP * ACK :draft/bot-cmds
< :irc.example.org CAP * ACK :obsidianirc/voice
< :irc.example.org 001 me :Welcome
< :irc.example.org 005 me CASEMAPPING=ascii CHANTYPES=#^$ PREFIX=(qaohv)~&@%+ CHANMODES=beI,k,l,imnpst WHOX :are supported
< :irc.example.org BATCH +c obsidianirc/cmdslist
< @batch=c :irc.example.org CMDSLIST +JOIN +PART +TOPIC +OPER
< :irc.example.org BATCH -c
< :irc.example.org CMDSLIST -OPER
< :me!u@host JOIN #obby
< :irc.example.org 354 me 332 #obby ident host.example alice H@ alice_acct :Alice Smith
< :irc.example.org PROP #obby +obsidianirc/censor +obsidianirc/history=30d
< @msgid=p1;time=2026-09-06T10:00:00.000Z :alice!u@host PRIVMSG #obby :look at https://example.org
< @+reply=p1;obsidianirc/link-preview-title=Example\sDomain;obsidianirc/link-preview-snippet=A\sdomain\sfor\sexamples :irc.example.org TAGMSG #obby
# The server-scope bots arrive as one batch on connect; a self-registered bot loses `oper`.
< :irc.example.org BATCH +b obby.world/channel-bots
< @batch=b;obby.world/bot-info=eyJldmVudCI6ImFkZCIsImJvdF9pZCI6ImIxIiwibmljayI6IndlYXRoZXJib3QiLCJmcm9tX2NvbmZpZyI6ZmFsc2UsImNoYW5uZWxzIjpbIiNvYmJ5Il0sImNvbW1hbmRzIjpbeyJuYW1lIjoiZm9yZWNhc3QiLCJkZXNjcmlwdGlvbiI6InRoZSB3ZWF0aGVyIn0seyJuYW1lIjoib3BlciJ9XX0= :irc.example.org TAGMSG me
< :irc.example.org BATCH -b
< @+draft/bot-cmds=eyJwcmVmaXgiOiIvIiwiY29tbWFuZHMiOlt7Im5hbWUiOiJmb3JlY2FzdCIsImRlc2NyaXB0aW9uIjoidGhlIHdlYXRoZXIifSx7Im5hbWUiOiJyYWRhciJ9XX0= :weatherbot!u@bot.obby.world TAGMSG me
# One WHOIS, wrapped in the vendor batch, with the per-session numerics in a batch of their own.
< :irc.example.org BATCH +w obby.world/whois alice
< @batch=w :irc.example.org BATCH +s obby.world/whois-session
< @batch=s :irc.example.org 671 me alice :is using a Secure Connection
< @batch=s :irc.example.org 317 me alice 42 1787477054 :seconds idle, signon time
< @batch=w :irc.example.org BATCH -s
< @batch=w :irc.example.org 311 me alice ident host.example * :Alice Smith
< @batch=w :irc.example.org 312 me alice irc.example.org :ObbyIRCd
< @batch=w :irc.example.org 319 me alice :~@#obby
< @batch=w :irc.example.org 330 me alice alice_acct :is logged in as
< @batch=w :irc.example.org 318 me alice :End of /WHOIS list.
< :irc.example.org BATCH -w
# The channel keeps everyone and everything it holds across a rename.
< :irc.example.org RENAME #obby #obby-world :tidying up
< :me!u@host JOIN ^general
< @+obsidianirc/rtc={"type":"join","channel":"^general"} :alice!u@host TAGMSG ^general
